{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":62,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":62,"text":"  difference            : 0/s","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":63,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":63,"text":"  the scope is identical and now costs nothing","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":64,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":64,"text":"  so the rule is not 'wide locks are slow'","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":65,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":65,"text":"  it is 'a lock costs the duration of what it covers, and a network call has","end":"\n"}
